    "description": "🃏 Grouped flashcard review and deck operations. Use the "action" field to select the operation.

Common actions: list_cards, get_decks, get_cards. Required fields: list_cards: scope, filter; get_decks: no additional fields; get_cards: deckID.

Additional actions: review_card, create_card, remove_card. Read siyuan://help/action/flashcard/{action} for details, or call action="help" if resources are unavailable.

Parameter contract per action (fields outside the action's optional list should not be sent):
flashcard.list_cards: required [scope, filter] | optional [deckID, notebook, rootID, reviewedCards]
flashcard.get_decks: required [] | optional []
flashcard.get_cards: required [deckID] | optional [page, pageSize]
flashcard.review_card: required [deckID, cardID] | optional [rating, skip, reviewedCards]
flashcard.create_card: required [deckID, blockIDs] | optional [mode]
flashcard.remove_card: required [deckID, blockIDs] | optional []

flashcard actions cover review-first flashcard workflows and deck discovery. list_cards always reads from the kernel due-card endpoints and MCP post-filters cards by state for filter="new" or filter="old"; pass reviewedCards to match SiYuan's in-review filtering. Requires user confirmation before: remove_card.",
    "overview": {
      "actionSummaries": {
        "create_card": "Use deckID + blockIDs to turn existing blocks into flashcards. Non-built-in deck IDs must already exist. This calls SiYuan's addRiffCards flow, which writes custom-riff-decks and creates deck records together.",
        "get_cards": "Use deckID + optional page/pageSize to list all cards in a deck (regardless of due state). Use empty string deckID to query across all decks. Returns cards, total count, and pageCount.",
        "get_decks": "Returns available flashcard decks so the caller can discover deckID values.",
        "list_cards": "Use scope="all" | "deck" | "notebook" | "tree" plus filter="due" | "new" | "old". For scope="all", omit deckID; an empty string is treated as omitted. For scope="deck", pass a non-empty deckID. For scope="notebook", pass notebook. For scope="tree", pass rootID. reviewedCards is optional and follows SiYuan's review flow.",
        "remove_card": "Use deckID + blockIDs to remove existing blocks from a deck. This action requires explicit user confirmation.",
        "review_card": "Use deckID + cardID + rating, or pass skip=true to skip. reviewedCards is optional; each entry must include cardID because SiYuan only reads reviewedCards[].cardID.",
      },
      "actions": {
        "create_card": {
          "hint": "Use deckID + blockIDs to turn existing blocks into flashcards. Non-built-in deck IDs must already exist. This calls SiYuan's addRiffCards flow, which writes custom-riff-decks and creates deck records together.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "get_cards": {
          "hint": "Use deckID + optional page/pageSize to list all cards in a deck (regardless of due state). Use empty string deckID to query across all decks. Returns cards, total count, and pageCount.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "get_decks": {
          "hint": "Returns available flashcard decks so the caller can discover deckID values.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "list_cards": {
          "hint": "Use scope="all" | "deck" | "notebook" | "tree" plus filter="due" | "new" | "old". For scope="all", omit deckID; an empty string is treated as omitted. For scope="deck", pass a non-empty deckID. For scope="notebook", pass notebook. For scope="tree", pass rootID. reviewedCards is optional and follows SiYuan's review flow.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "remove_card": {
          "hint": "Use deckID + blockIDs to remove existing blocks from a deck. This action requires explicit user confirmation.",
          "requiresConfirmation": true,
