    "description": "📂 Simplified filesystem-style document operations. Use the "action" field to select the operation.

Common actions: ls, tree, read, write, replace, search. Required fields: ls: path; tree: path; read: path; write: path, markdown; replace: path, edit; search: path, query.

Additional actions: rm, mv. Read siyuan://help/action/fs/{action} for details, or call action="help" if resources are unavailable.

Parameter contract per action (fields outside the action's optional list should not be sent):
fs.ls: required [path] | optional []
fs.tree: required [path] | optional [maxDepth]
fs.read: required [path] | optional [page, pageSize]
fs.write: required [path, markdown] | optional [overwrite]
fs.replace: required [path, edit] | optional []
fs.rm: required [path] | optional []
fs.mv: required [from, to] | optional []
fs.search: required [path, query] | optional [regex, caseSensitive, page, pageSize]

Use fs first for ordinary document file operations: list, tree, read, write, move, delete, and grep-like search. fs paths are human-readable workspace paths such as /Notebook/Folder/Doc; fs outputs the same human-readable path shape and hides notebook IDs, block IDs, and storage paths. Requires user confirmation before: rm, mv.",
    "overview": {
      "actionSummaries": {
        "ls": "Use a human-readable path. "/" lists readable notebook roots; /Notebook or /Notebook/Folder lists direct child documents.",
        "mv": "Moves or renames a document using human-readable paths. This action requires explicit user confirmation.",
        "read": "Use a human-readable document path. Returns Markdown content only, with pagination for long documents.",
        "replace": "Edits one existing document by exact old/new string matching. edit accepts one object or an array for sequential replacements. replace_all=true replaces every exact match of that old snippet.",
        "rm": "Deletes a document by human-readable path. This action requires explicit user confirmation.",
        "search": "Searches Markdown lines under a human-readable document or folder path. Use regex=true for regular expressions.",
        "tree": "Use a human-readable path. maxDepth defaults to 3 and keeps output compact.",
        "write": "Creates a missing document. Existing documents are protected unless overwrite=true; overwrite replaces the body while preserving the document node and title.",
      },
      "actions": {
        "ls": {
          "hint": "Use a human-readable path. "/" lists readable notebook roots; /Notebook or /Notebook/Folder lists direct child documents.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "mv": {
